# Runtime dependencies for the Vercel Python function.
#
# This path is not decorative: @vercel/python installs from the requirements
# file beside the entrypoint. Named anything else, the root requirements.txt is
# used instead and the bundle silently gains pytest and Streamlit.
#
# Narrower than requirements-runtime.in, which is the container's set: a
# serverless bundle has a size limit and a cold start, and this path needs
# neither a server (Vercel provides it) nor alembic (migrations are run
# separately, never by the function). The reasoning provider on a deployment
# like this is `deterministic` -- no credential, no outbound call -- so the
# Anthropic SDK is not here either. Add it back and set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY to
# use the model path.
#
# Pinned at the same versions as the other sets. A deployment resolving to a
# different SQLAlchemy from the one CI tested is a difference nobody would see
# until it mattered.
#
# Regenerate:
#   uv pip compile api/requirements.in --generate-hashes --python-version 3.12 \
#       -o api/requirements.txt
fastapi==0.141.1
sqlalchemy==2.0.52
psycopg2-binary==2.9.12
pydantic==2.13.4
pydantic-settings==2.15.0
pyyaml==6.0.3
